-- title:
--   Divisibility of Pic⁰ in characteristic p
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, let $K$ be algebraically closed, and let $p$ be a natural number that is prime and is the characteristic of $K$; the prime $p$ enters only through this characteristic hypothesis. Assume the finiteness hypothesis `hfg`: there is an $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$. Assume further `IsCurveOver K F`, that is: every nonzero $f \in F$ has an associated divisor (a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on the set of places of $F/K$, a place being a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring) whose value at each place $v$ is $v.ord f$ and whose degree is $0$; every residue field of a place is a finite-dimensional $K$-module; and the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one over $F$. Then for every natural number $n \neq 0$ and every class $x$ in $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/K)$, the group of degree-zero divisors modulo principal divisors, there exists $y$ in $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/K)$ with $n \cdot y = x$.
--
--   This is the divisibility of the degree-zero divisor class group of a one-variable function field over an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, classically the surjectivity of multiplication by $n$ on the $K$-points of the Jacobian, including the case $p \mid n$ where the isogeny is inseparable. It is the positive-characteristic counterpart of the characteristic-zero divisibility statement and is used in the project's counting of torsion in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$, in the Abel–Jacobi cardinality results, and in the comparison of torsion under constant reduction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Pic0_exists_nsmul_eq_of_charP.lean

import Mathlib
